olor=&#8221;#2a98ac&#8221; text_orientation=&#8221;center&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;||||false|false&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;||||false|false&#8221;]<\/p>\n<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\">WHO WE ARE<\/h1>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][\/et_pb_column][\/et_pb_row][\/et_pb_section][et_pb_section fb_built=&#8221;1&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; background_color=&#8221;#2a98ac&#8221; max_height=&#8221;100px&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;0px||||false|false&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;0px||69px|68px|false|false&#8221;][\/et_pb_section][et_pb_section fb_built=&#8221;1&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; background_color=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;0px||||false|false&#8221; link_option_url=&#8221;\/home\/&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;][et_pb_row _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; background_color=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; width=&#8221;95%&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;7px||||false|false&#8221;][et_pb_column type=&#8221;4_4&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243;][et_pb_text _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|800|||||||&#8221; header_text_align=&#8221;center&#8221; header_text_color=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; background_color=&#8221;#2a98ac&#8221; width=&#8221;100%&#8221; max_width=&#8221;1080px&#8221; module_alignment=&#8221;center&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;0px||||false|false&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;0px|0px||0px|false|true&#8221; header_text_shadow_style=&#8221;preset1&#8243; border_width_all=&#8221;6px&#8221; border_color_all=&#8221;#2a98ac&#8221;]<\/p>\n<h1>STAFF<\/h1>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Elvy Crane &#8211; Director, Internal Operations&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/06\/Elvy-1-150&#215;150.jpg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>Elvy learned about WPV through a neighbor and started out as a volunteer.\u00a0\u00a0She has loved being involved with WPV ever since and joined the staff in 2014.\u00a0\u00a0As the primary contact for our members, Elvy enjoys talking with them to coordinate their transportation needs, friendly visits, errands and other service requests.\u00a0\u00a0Elvy works closely with our volunteers to match their schedules and interests with client requests.\u00a0\u00a0She also enjoys planning WPV social events.\u00a0\u00a0Elvy and her family have been residents of Westchester for 20 years.\u00a0\u00a0She enjoys entertaining, cooking, music, and movies.<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Diane Wade &#8211; Director, Programs and Community Development&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/07\/DianeWade-150&#215;150.jpeg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>Diane is a marketing professional with over 25 years of experience in brand management and communications in the health and wellness industry. She started at WPV as a volunteer before becoming a consultant overseeing WPV programs, communications and community outreach. A Culver City resident, she is a member of the Rotary Club, a Culver City Education Foundation Ambassador and volunteers at the Culver City Senior Center, She and her daughter moved from New York to California 11 years ago. She received a BA in Economics from Georgetown and an MBA in Marketing from the University of Michigan Ross School of Business.<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Natalie Noel &#8211; Associate Director of Programs and Special Projects&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/06\/Image-6-4-25-at-11.47-AM-150&#215;150.jpeg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Natalie first worked with WPV back in 2014 and has stayed connected with us over the years. With 15 years of experience as a Human Resources Manager at a design and architecture firm, and is also a trained end-of-life doula, providing compassionate support to individuals and families navigating life\u2019s final transitions. Natalie and her husband are residents of Torrance.<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_text _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|800|||||||&#8221; header_text_align=&#8221;center&#8221; header_text_color=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; background_color=&#8221;#2a98ac&#8221; width=&#8221;100%&#8221; max_width=&#8221;1080px&#8221; module_alignment=&#8221;center&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;0px||||false|false&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;0px|0px||0px|false|true&#8221; header_text_shadow_style=&#8221;preset1&#8243; border_width_all=&#8221;6px&#8221; border_color_all=&#8221;#2a98ac&#8221;]<\/p>\n<h1>BOARD OF DIRECTORS<\/h1>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Rich Crane &#8211; Co-Treasurer&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/06\/Image-6-4-25-at-11.48-AM-150&#215;150.jpeg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">Rich is a long-time Westchester resident and staunch supporter of WPV. A graduate of Loyola Marymount University, Rich has over 30 years of experience in the hospitality management industry building and leading high-performance teams across multiple sectors. He is a visionary leader who drives growth and innovation to deliver outstanding results for his clients and community stakeholders, and is the current Executive Vice President of PMP, a prestigious HOA Management and Consulting firm.<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Joan Holowaty &#8211; Member&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/10\/image-120&#215;150-2.png&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">Joan Holowaty became a Villager during her husband&#8217;s terminal illness in 2018. They had recently moved here from the Washington DC area to welcome their first grandchild.\u00a0 Forever grateful for the caring support her family received, she has been a WPV member and volunteer ever since. Professionally, Joan has over 35 years experience as a marketing\/ sales executive with Verizon\u00a0 Communications and as founder and President of her marketing consulting firm. Originally from NYC, Joan received her BA in English from Hunter College of City University of New York.\u00a0 Current hobbies include gardening, reading and most importantly, spoiling her two granddaughters!<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Carol Kitabayashi &#8211; Co-Chair&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/02\/carolwebphoto.jpg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>Carol served as WPV\u2019s Executive Director for 10+ year from 2011 to 2021. During that time, she was instrumental in helping the organization establish roots, grow, expand, and flourish. She developed the WPV CARES (COVID-19 Action Response for Elder Support) Program that ran for nearly 2 years during the pandemic. Over 200 WPV clients received much needed support and assistance from over 300 volunteers through this free program. Carol has helped other villages get started in the L.A. County area and has been a strong advocate for the village model nationally. \u00a0She serves on the Board of Directors for Village Movement California, a statewide coalition of villages dedicated to bringing visibility to the benefits and value of villages. \u00a0Carol and her husband are long-time residents of both the Westchester and Culver City area.<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Carin Mavrosakis &#8211; Co-Chair&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/02\/Carin.jpg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]Carin Mavrosakis is a Director of Compensation,<strong><em>\u00a0<\/em><\/strong>Talent Development and Training and Learning at Toyota North America with 20 years of corporate business experience as a Human Resources Professional. Carin has a passion for volunteering and helping those in need.\u00a0 She volunteers often through Toyota in her local community, mentoring underprivileged youth and has a passion for the caring of seniors in her family and community.\u00a0 Carin holds a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Human Resources Management from Cal State Long Beach; she is a<strong><em>\u00a0<\/em><\/strong>Texas\/California native with her husband and two sons.<br \/>\n[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Jody Onorato &#8211; Secretary&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/10\/image-120&#215;150-1.png&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>Jody joined WPV as a vetted service provider nearly ten years ago and shortly afterwards became an enthusiastic volunteer as well. This was the same year she became involved in navigating and providing care for her ailing mother and became acutely aware of the challenges of findingthe support that was needed to assure safety and pece of mind. Born and raised in the Los Angeles area, she earned her BA in English Literature at CSUN, while working full-time managing a medical practice. She has been a docent at local nature centers, enjoys, gardening, traveling, visiting museums, cooking and never turns down an offer to try out the offerings at a new ethnic restaurant.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Attellia (Tia) Otten  &#8211; Co-Treasurer&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/02\/TiaOtten.jpg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">Tia is a long time resident of Playa Del Rey, having moved there after graduating from Oregon State University. She\u00a0is a retiree\u00a0from a major defense contractor where she was a Senior Manager in Engineering. She has strong program and project management experience and her expertise has been instrumental in helping to grow our organization. Tia is a former member of Westchester Rotary Club and\u00a0the Westchester Family YMCA Board of Managers, and is a member of the Woman&#8217;s\u00a0Club of Playa del Rey and\u00a0P.E.O., a philanthropic educational organization.<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Peter Palmer &#8211; Member&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/10\/image-120&#215;150-1-1.png&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">Peter was born and raised in the Crenshaw District\/View Park\/Windsor Hills areas of Los Angeles. He attended Loyola High School, USC, and The University of West Los Angeles School of Law. He served as a Deputy Public Defender for 27 years and was granted a service-connected disability retirement in 2004. His passion in retirement has been chorale singing, presently with The Concert Singers of Westchester and The Space Park Chorale of Manhattan Beach. He became aware of WPV in 2018 when he had foot surgery, and became a Member to get rides to the doctor. He was so impressed with WPV&#8217;s mission that he became a Volunteer and Donor. He called himself a triple threat&#8230;.now a quadruple threat, as he has been honored to become a Director of the Board of WPV.<\/p>\n<div class=\"yj6qo\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Kathy Van Ness &#8211; Member&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243; locked=&#8221;off&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/11\/Screenshot-2025-11-13-at-4.19.14\u202fPM-150&#215;150.png&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">Kathy is almost a native of Westchester though she was born in Texas. She attended schools in California, Washington and Ohio. She worked in health care before switching to the public sector. Kathy worked for almost 25 years at Los Angeles World Airports where she specialized in strategic planning and budgeting. She also worked at Long Beach Airport, and has taught financial management in a Master of Public Administration program. Since retiring, Kathy has become active in nonprofits. In addition to serving on the Board of WPV, she serves on the Executive and Finance Committees of The Holland Society of New York and on the Board of the West Los Angeles College Foundation. <\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Diane Wade &#8211; Director, Programs and Community Development&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/07\/DianeWade-150&#215;150.jpeg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>Diane is a marketing professional with over 25 years of experience in brand management and communications in the health and wellness industry. She started at WPV as a volunteer before becoming a consultant overseeing WPV programs, communications and community outreach. A Culver City resident, she is a member of the Rotary Club, a Culver City Education Foundation Ambassador and volunteers at the Culver City Senior Center, She and her daughter moved from New York to California 11 years ago. She received a BA in Economics from Georgetown and an MBA in Marketing from the University of Michigan Ross School of Business.<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][et_pb_team_member name=&#8221;Morrey Plotkin &#8211; Chairman Emeritus&#8221; image_url=&#8221;https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/02\/Morrey_Plotkin.jpg&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; header_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; locked=&#8221;off&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p class=\"p1\">Well-known and respected in the community for his philanthropic activies and contributions, Morrey was instrumental in securing funding for WPV at a critical time in the organization&#8217;s startup phase. He also helped make important connections to key leaders in the community that gave the non-profit the support it needed to continue growing.<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_team_member][\/et_pb_column][\/et_pb_row][\/et_pb_section][et_pb_section fb_built=&#8221;1&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; custom_margin=&#8221;0px||0px||false|false&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;0px||0px||false|false&#8221; global_module=&#8221;2619&#8243; saved_tabs=&#8221;all&#8221; collapsed=&#8221;off&#8221;][et_pb_row _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; width=&#8221;50%&#8221; module_alignment=&#8221;center&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;0px||||false|false&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;0px||0px||false|false&#8221;][et_pb_column type=&#8221;4_4&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243;][et_pb_code _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243;]<\/p>\n<div id=\"mc_embed_shell\"><!-- [et_pb_line_break_holder] -->      <link href=\"\/\/cdn-images.mailchimp.com\/embedcode\/classic-061523.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text\/css\"><!-- [et_pb_line_break_holder] -->  <\/p>\n<style type=\"text\/css\"><!-- [et_pb_line_break_holder] -->        #mc_embed_signup{background:#fff; false;clear:left; font:14px Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; width: 600px;}<!-- [et_pb_line_break_holder] -->        \/* Add your own Mailchimp form style overrides in your site stylesheet or in this style block.<!-- [et_pb_line_break_holder] -->           We recommend moving this block and the preceding CSS link to the HEAD of your HTML file. *\/<!-- [et_pb_line_break_holder] --><\/style>\n<p><!-- [et_pb_line_break_holder] --><